Subject: [PATCH] Synchronization: annotate Linux futex mutex for TSan

The Linux Synchronization.Mutex implementation uses Swift Atomics and direct
futex syscalls rather than an intercepted pthread primitive. The installed
ThreadSanitizer runtime therefore cannot observe the mutex acquire/release
edges and reports every correctly protected inout access as a race.

Use libswiftCore's process-wide TSan hook pointers through
_SynchronizationShims and invoke them after a successful lock acquisition and
before release. A direct weak import is not sufficient: because Mutex is
@_alwaysEmitIntoClient, the non-TSan standard-library build can fold that weak
symbol check away before the body reaches an instrumented client. The runtime
hook pointers remain externally visible and are populated by
__tsan_on_initialize, so a predicted-cold null check preserves ordinary links
while instrumented clients receive the same happens-before relation that TSan
derives automatically for pthread_mutex_lock/unlock.

Sentinel: NUCLEUS_SWIFT_SOURCE_LINUX_MUTEX_TSAN

diff --git a/stdlib/public/SwiftShims/swift/shims/_SynchronizationShims.h b/stdlib/public/SwiftShims/swift/shims/_SynchronizationShims.h
index bb3477bca56..b08c113db30 100644
--- a/stdlib/public/SwiftShims/swift/shims/_SynchronizationShims.h
+++ b/stdlib/public/SwiftShims/swift/shims/_SynchronizationShims.h
@@ -24,0 +25,27 @@
+// NUCLEUS_SWIFT_SOURCE_LINUX_MUTEX_TSAN: The Linux Mutex is implemented
+// directly with atomics and futex syscalls, so ThreadSanitizer cannot infer
+// its acquire/release edges from an intercepted pthread primitive. Use the
+// libswiftCore hook pointers rather than weak direct imports: this header is
+// serialized into @_alwaysEmitIntoClient bodies during a non-TSan stdlib
+// build, where a weak direct-symbol check can be folded away before an
+// instrumented client sees it.
+#if defined(__cplusplus)
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+extern void (*_swift_tsan_acquire)(const void *);
+extern void (*_swift_tsan_release)(const void *);
+#if defined(__cplusplus)
+} // extern "C"
+#endif
+
+static inline void _swift_stdlib_tsan_acquire(void *addr) {
+  if (__builtin_expect(!!_swift_tsan_acquire, 0)) {
+    _swift_tsan_acquire(addr);
+  }
+}
+
+static inline void _swift_stdlib_tsan_release(void *addr) {
+  if (__builtin_expect(!!_swift_tsan_release, 0)) {
+    _swift_tsan_release(addr);
+  }
+}
+
